SECTION 8: LANGUAGE EVOLUTION IN RAPIDITY TIME
==============================================================================

If we use rapidity time tau = ln(t)/2 where t = years before present,
then exponential processes become LINEAR in tau.

Hypothesis: language branching events are approximately uniform
in rapidity time (like biological speciation events in log-time).

